# LADAKH SHELTER OPTIMIZER - COMPLETE RESOURCE DATABASE

## CLIMATE DATA SOURCES
1. NASA POWER API
   - Link: https://power.larc.nasa.gov/
   - Description: 40+ years of global climate data
   - Parameters: Temperature, Solar Irradiance, Wind

2. India Meteorological Department
   - Link: https://mausam.imd.gov.in/
   - Leh Station Data: Available on request

3. NREL NSRDB
   - Link: https://nsrdb.nrel.gov/
   - Solar radiation data for India

## SOFTWARE REPOSITORIES
1. PyMAPDL (ANSYS Python Interface)
   - GitHub: https://github.com/ansys/pymapdl
   - Docs: https://mapdl.docs.pyansys.com/

2. pvlib-python (Solar Modeling)
   - GitHub: https://github.com/pvlib/pvlib-python
   - Docs: https://pvlib-python.readthedocs.io/

3. FiPy (PDE Solver)
   - GitHub: https://github.com/usnistgov/fipy
   - Docs: https://www.ctcms.nist.gov/fipy/

## RESEARCH PAPERS
1. "Passive Solar Architecture in Cold Climates" - GERES
   - Download: https://www.geres.eu/en/projects/

2. "Thermal Performance of Ladakhi Houses" - Singh et al. (2009)
   - DOI: 10.1016/j.enbuild.2009.06.009

3. "Solar Passive Building Design" - Chel & Tiwari (2010)
   - DOI: 10.1016/j.rser.2009.10.005

## MATERIAL DATABASES
1. ASHRAE Handbook - Fundamentals
   - Link: https://www.ashrae.org/

2. MatWeb Material Property Database
   - Link: http://www.matweb.com/

3. BIS Indian Standards
   - IS 3792:1978, IS 1725:2013
   - Link: https://www.services.bis.gov.in/

## VALIDATION TOOLS
1. EnergyPlus (DOE Building Simulator)
   - Link: https://energyplus.net/
   - Validation datasets included

2. TRNSYS (Transient Simulation)
   - Link: http://www.trnsys.com/

## DEPLOYMENT RESOURCES
1. Docker Hub - Python Images
   - Link: https://hub.docker.com/_/python

2. Heroku Deployment Guide
   - Link: https://devcenter.heroku.com/

3. AWS EC2 ANSYS Setup
   - Link: https://aws.amazon.com/hpc/